   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">PAJ - Annual Narrative Report 2025</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">The 2025 programmatic exercise marked a qualitative leap in the materialisation of the Promoting Access to Justice (PAJ) Program, consolidating itself as a robust institutional response sensitive to the crisis context affecting the provinces of Cabo Delgado and Nampula. The operationalisation of the delegations of the Ombudsman&apos;s Office and the National Human Rights Commission in Pemba represented more than just a physical expansion; it signified the re-establishment of the State&apos;s presence as a guarantor of rights in areas of extreme vulnerability.Through proximity justice, the program succeeded in breaking the silence of populations that, until then, remained invisible to the formal system, transforming community grievances into legal processes of reparation and dignity. The effectiveness of the PAJ in 2025 lay in its ability to coordinate a complex network of actors, from the Office of the Female Parliamentarian and central Government instances to religious leaders and community journalists at the grassroots. This synergy allowed the protection of displaced women and girls to evolve from a fragmented agenda into a transversal imperative in public policies and real-time human rights monitoring.</narrative>
   </description>
